            <ArticleTitle>Intraligamentary injection of slow-release methylprednisolone for the prevention of pain after endodontic treatment.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>651-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The intraligamentary injection of a slow-release steroidal, the anti-inflammatory agent slow-release methylprednisolone (Depomedrol), was compared to a placebo and to an active placebo (Mepivacaine) in preventing postoperative pain after root canal treatment. The results clearly demonstrated that the tested drug significantly reduced the frequency and intensity of postoperative pain sequelae in the experimental set-up.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
